  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // ADDENDUM 2026-08-03 (Claude, live during task #3 / Ax_TraceabilityClosure
  // investigation) — axiom-ID collision extends into DEPLOYED CODE, not just docs
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  code_level_findings: [
    { id: "CODE1", severity: "high", tag: "CONTRADICTION", status: "OPEN, NOT YET REMEDIATED",
      what: "docs/internal/PLAN.md defines a completely separate 'Tier α —
          Internal hardening (Priorities A0..A4)' roadmap -- an engineering
          task checklist, unrelated to the philosophical axiom system:
          A0='s3_star.rs anti-capture audit sampling' (2-4h), A1='Arc<RwLock
          <NucleusConfig>> threaded to S4' (1-2h), A2='S5 boot-time covenant
          verify with fail-closed' (1-2h), A3='Algedonic synthetic exercise
          harness' (1-2h), A4='Witness signature scaffolding' (2-3h). These
          bare 'A<n>' labels appear DIRECTLY in live, deployed Rust source:
          projects/vsf-nucleus/src/s5.rs:4,47 ('Tier α A2' header comment,
          '/// A4 — Witnesses configured for multi-party covenant
          attestation'), main.rs:53,7914 ('mod s5; // A2 — S5 boot-time
          covenant verify...'). Worse than the doc-only CT1/CT3 collisions
          already fixed: 'A0' means the project's most sacred, ungovernable
          ethical axiom (covenant.vsm) in one place and a 2-4h engineering
          task in another, in the SAME source tree an engineer maintaining
          the nucleus reads directly. Discovered while checking whether A4
          (no sibling coupling) has real code enforcement worth adding to
          Ax_TraceabilityClosure -- adding it naively would have pointed
          'A4: enforced_by s5.rs#...' at witness-verification code, not
          sibling-coupling enforcement, actively worsening the exact
          confusion this whole audit exists to fix." },
  ],

  code_level_recommendation: "Before Ax_TraceabilityClosure's scope question
      (open_questions, 3rd item) can be safely resolved, PLAN.md's Tier α
      roadmap IDs need to stop reusing bare 'A<n>' -- rename to something
      disambiguated (e.g. 'Tα.0'..'Tα.4') so 'A0'..'A4' in source code and
      docs means ONLY the philosophical axiom, everywhere. rmw3 2026-08-03:
      this deeper thread ('hasta donde tira la hebra' -- how far the
      collision actually extends across the codebase, not just the 5 PLAN.md
