      the queued-not-dispatched status.",

  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // CROSS-CUTTING PATTERN
  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  pattern: "Two independent audits (disjoint file sets, no shared context)
      converged on the SAME shape of problem without coordinating: (a) an
      axiom ID gets redefined across the 'canonical' tier (A5 x3, A8 x2,
      D7 x2 — found independently by BOTH forks), (b) axioms cited as
      binding in operational docs (RULES.md, systems/*.md) trace back to a
      'working'-tier doc (concepts.md) rather than the 'canonical'-tier
      covenant, breaking the covenant's own closure claim, (c) at least one
      'canonical' doc (S3_control.md) is directly contradicted by deployed,
      running code and has been for a month, undetected, because nothing
      reads these docs. This is the SAME root pattern already named earlier
      this session for the CLAUDE.md dead-link finding: a fix or a doc that
      LOOKS complete/authoritative because nothing ever exercises it against
      reality. R9 (no silent concessions) and the doc-sync-discipline
      practice in RULES.md exist for exactly this, but neither one currently
      has a mechanism that reaches axiom definitions specifically.",

  // ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  // OPEN QUESTIONS — reserved for rmw3 (S5), NOT decided here
